<title>USA: CBS names Aber vice president of cable unit.</title>
<headline>CBS names Aber vice president of cable unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>CBS, a unit of Westinghouse Electric Corp, said it named Bill Aber as vice president for new business development at its cable division, a new post.</p>
<p>Aber was previously vice president and general manager of WBZ-TV in Boston. Aber was replaced by Ed Goldman, who was vice president and general manager of WBZ Radio.</p>
